  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing (NAICS 339112) has recorded $126M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The market awarded 770 contracts with an average award size of $163K. Obligations fell 88.6% year over year. Fiscal-year totals before FY2027 were larger: FY22 $1.1B, FY23 $1.6B, FY24 $2B, FY25 $1.6B, and FY26 $1.1B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer in FY2027 to date, obligating $123M. The Department of Justice obligated $2.3M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $215K. WELCH ALLYN, INC. is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $31.6M, followed by OLYMPUS AMERICA INC with $25.4M and SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC with $11.9M. The data show a concentrated buyer base and a small set of suppliers capturing the largest shares of the reduced FY2027 obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is FY2027 federal demand for NAICS 339112?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $123M in FY2027 to date, making VA the dominant buyer. The Department of Justice and the Department of Health and Human Services follow at much smaller scales with $2.3M and $215K respectively. The top vendors capture a large share of obligations, led by WELCH ALLYN, INC. with $31.6M and OLYMPUS AMERICA INC with $25.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 activity compare with prior years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations are $126M versus prior fiscal-year totals of FY22 $1.1B, FY23 $1.6B, FY24 $2B, FY25 $1.6B, and FY26 $1.1B. Obligations fell 88.6% year over year. The count of awards is 770 with an average award size of $163K, reflecting smaller or fewer awards compared with prior full fiscal years."
      }
    ]
  },
